Wuhan, lease, noise-related rent reduction, service fee');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_2b8174ae','(2023) E 0102 Civil First-Instance No. 15618','Qintai Huating Deposit-Refund Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_jiangan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-01-23','Tenant Zhou, Landlord Xu','Qintai Huating deposit return dispute: The landlord withheld the deposit on the grounds of deep cleaning, with the disputed amount approximately 22,930 yuan.','Regarding the Qintai Huating property, both parties acknowledge that the landlord withheld the deposit on the grounds of deep cleaning; because the parties had previously tried to coordinate through the property management company but failed to reach an agreement, they were unable to agree on how the deposit, repair, or service costs should be allocated.','The transfer records and handover photographs in the Qintai Huating case file corroborate one another with the time records. On this basis, the court held that traces of normal use cannot automatically be deemed damage and strictly scrutinized promises made by the parties that were not included in the contract.','The court held in the Qintai Huating case that normal signs of use cannot automatically be deemed damage, and that key costs and living conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Qintai Huating: return the portion of the deposit corresponding to losses that have not been proven; the established losses shall be counted toward liability in the amount of 1210 yuan, and the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Mediation','Wuhan, Rental, Deposit Refund, Accessibility');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_8a467436','(2025) E 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 26593','Qintai Neighborhood Maintenance Liability Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-02-07','Tenant Gu, landlord Han','Qintai Neighborhood maintenance liability dispute: After water seepage occurred in the bathroom, the parties disagreed over the repair deadline; the disputed amount was approximately 12,226 yuan.','This case arose from the repair-responsibility issue after the handover of Qintai Block. The tenant submitted materials alleging that, after water seepage in the bathroom, the parties disagreed over the repair deadline, while the landlord explained its handling by stating that “the tenant promptly sent written notice after discovering the problem.”','Regarding the repair liability issue at Qintai Block, the court relied primarily on repair requests and on-site inspection reports, while considering the condition at handover and subsequent remedial measures; a landlord who, after becoming aware of the issue, fails to make timely repairs should bear the corresponding liability.','The Qintai Neighborhood case confirmed that a landlord who, after becoming aware of the issue, fails to carry out repairs promptly should bear corresponding liability, and that the door width, repair costs, and service fees at issue should all be determined based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the Qintai neighborhood dispute, the court ordered the responsible party to bear the repair costs and compensate for reasonable losses. The amount supported by documentation was determined to be 1365 yuan, and the remaining claims will be handled separately.','Partial support','Wuhan, rental, repair responsibility, deposit');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_f7af9c74','(2025) E 0106 Civil First Instance No. 2253','Qintai Neighborly Entrance Door-Width Description Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-08-05','Tenant Chen and landlord Wu','Qintai Neighborly entrance door-width description dispute: The intermediary verbally promised a certain entrance door width, but the measurements at handover did not match; the disputed amount was approximately 19,260 yuan.','After moving into Qintai Linli, tenant Chen claimed that the agent had verbally promised a certain entrance-door width, but the measurement at handover did not match. During the handover at Qintai Linli, the parties attempted to resolve the matter through the property management office but failed to reach an agreement, leading them to disagree over the timing of notice and the scope of the costs.','Regarding Qintai Linli, the court examined chat records and photographs measuring the doorway width. These materials establish the course of the transaction. In light of the sequence in which the parties performed, it may be found that key residential conditions forming the basis of the contract should have been truthfully disclosed; oral statements not supported by other evidence are not treated as the primary basis.','The key holding is that essential residential conditions should be truthfully disclosed when they form the basis of the contract; in a Qintai neighborhood rental, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadlines cannot be based solely on oral statements.','The Qintai Neighborly Entrance Door-Width Description matter was ultimately handled by “refunding the service fee and adjusting liability for breach of contract.” Upon calculation, the supported amount was 703 yuan; the portion beyond the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, door width details, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_7af1c245','(2025) E01 Civil First-Instance No. 19788','Contract dispute case concerning the Qintai Courtyard elevator shutdown','court_wh_intermediate','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-04-01','Tenant Tang, Landlord Jiang','Qintai Courtyard elevator shutdown dispute: The prolonged shutdown of the elevator in a high-rise residential building affected normal use, with the disputed amount approximately 28,209 yuan.','After the tenancy relationship at Qintai Courtyard was established, the issue arose that “the prolonged shutdown of the elevator in a high-rise residential building affected normal use.” The agency was unable to provide complete records of the service process, and the tenant and landlord subsequently each submitted evidence regarding the written appendices and actual losses.','In hearing the dispute over the elevator shutdown at Qintai Xiaoyuan, the collegial panel first verified the property management notices and maintenance records, then compared the contract appendices with the notice records. Based on the evidence currently available, rent may be reduced at the court’s discretion when the continuing shutdown has affected the habitability of the premises, and liability should be allocated according to the actual impact.','The court held in the Qintai Xiaoyuan case that rent may be reduced at the court’s discretion when a continuous service outage reaches a level that affects habitability, and that key costs and living conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Qintai Xiaoyuan: reduce part of the rent for the period affected; the established losses shall be counted toward liability in the amount of 5132 yuan, and the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Rejected','Wuhan, rental, elevator outage, repairs');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_2caa4d1a','(2024) E0102 Civil First-Instance No. 13396','Qintai Residential Compound Pathway-Occupation Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_jiangan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-12-24','Tenant Luo, Landlord Ye','Qintai Residential Compound pathway-occupation dispute: A public ramp was repeatedly occupied by electric bicycles and miscellaneous items, with the disputed amount approximately 5450 yuan.','Regarding the Qintai Residential Area property, both parties acknowledge that the public ramp was repeatedly occupied by electric bicycles and miscellaneous items; because the agent failed to provide complete records of the service process, the parties were unable to agree on how the deposit, repair, or service costs should be allocated.','In the Qintai Residential Compound case file, on-site videos, property-management complaint records, and time records corroborate one another. On that basis, the court held that the management party should have taken reasonable cleanup measures after receiving the report and conducted strict scrutiny of the parties’ commitments that were not written into the contract.','The Qintai Residential Compound case confirmed that the management party should have taken reasonable cleanup measures after receiving the report; the issues involving door width, repairs, and service fees should all be determined based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the dispute concerning the Qintai residential area, the court ordered cleanup within a specified period and improvements to inspections; the amount supported by documentation was determined to be 4468 yuan, with the remaining claims addressed separately.','Rejected','Wuhan, rental, passageway obstruction, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_ddbfe89c','(2025) Hubei 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 9079','Contract dispute case concerning the Qintai Dormitory agency service fee','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-01-02','Tenant Xu, Landlord Shen','Qintai Dormitory agency service fee dispute: After the agreement was not concluded, the agency charged the full service fee, with the disputed amount approximately 15,999 yuan.','This case arose from the agency-service-fee issue after the handover of Qintai Dormitory. The tenant submitted materials alleging that the agent charged the full service fee after the contract signing fell through, while the landlord explained its handling by stating that “the tenant promptly sent written notice after discovering the problem.”','Regarding the brokerage service fee issue at Qintai Dormitory, the court relied primarily on the service agreement and property-viewing records, while considering the condition at handover and subsequent remedial measures; when the service has not been fully performed, the fee should be determined based on the actual amount of work completed.','The key point of the ruling is that when services have not been fully performed, the fees should be determined based on the actual amount of work completed; in the Qintai Dormitory lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadlines cannot rely solely on oral statements.','The Qintai Dormitory agency service fee matter was ultimately resolved by “refunding service fees that were not actually incurred.” Upon calculation, the supported amount was 8,018 yuan; the portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, agency service fee, service fee');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_62e7c551','(2024) E 0106 Civil First-Instance No. 14158','Qintai Yating Early Lease Termination Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-11-25','Tenant Han, landlord Lin','Qintai Yating early lease termination dispute: The tenant requested early termination because of changes in living conditions; the disputed amount was approximately 25,553 yuan.','After moving into Qintai Yating, tenant Han claimed that the tenant sought early termination because the living conditions had changed. During the handover at Qintai Yating, the agent was unable to provide complete records of the service process, and the parties consequently disagreed over the notification timing and the scope of the costs.','Regarding Qintai Yating, the court examined the contract attachments and correspondence emails. These materials establish the course of the transaction. In light of the sequence in which the parties performed, it may be found that a penalty for breach that is excessively high when the losses are limited may be adjusted in accordance with the law; oral statements not supported by other evidence are not treated as the primary basis.','The court held in the Qintai Yating case that liquidated damages may be adjusted in accordance with the law when they are excessively high and the losses are limited, and that key costs and living conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Qintai Yating: assume appropriate liability based on the actual losses; the established losses shall be counted toward liability in the amount of 13965 yuan, and the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Rejected','Wuhan, Early Lease Termination, Repairs');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_27169220','(2024) E 01 Civil First Instance No. 23338','Qintai Chunxiao Identity Document Materials Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_intermediate','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-11-17','Tenant Wu, Landlord Zhou','Qintai Chunxiao identity document materials dispute: The intermediary requested too many photos of identification documents before signing the contract, and the disputed amount was approximately 35,512 yuan.','After the rental relationship at Qintai Chunxiao was established, an issue arose in which the intermediary had requested too many photos of identification documents before signing the contract. The intermediary was unable to provide complete records of the service process, and the tenant and landlord subsequently each submitted evidence concerning the written attachments and actual losses.','In hearing the dispute over identity materials at Qintai Chunxiao, the collegial panel first verified the information-collection page and chat records, then compared the contract appendices with the notice records. Based on the evidence currently available, rental verification should follow the principles of clear purpose and minimum necessity, and liability should be allocated according to the actual impact.','Confirmation of the Qintai Chunxiao case: Lease verification should follow the principles of clearly defined purpose and minimum necessity, and the issues involving door width, repairs, and service fees should all be determined based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the dispute concerning Qintai Chunxiao, the court ordered the deletion of irrelevant materials and an end to further processing; the amount supported by documentation was determined to be 14907 yuan, with the remaining claims addressed separately.','Support','Wuhan, rental, identity documents, service fee');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_e4d842fe','(2025) E0102 Civil First Instance No. 3746','Qintai Heyuan written attachment contract dispute case','court_wh_jiangan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-11-13','Tenant Jiang, Landlord Gu','Qintai Heyuan written attachment dispute: The parties disputed oral promises concerning ramp repairs and cleaning fees, with the disputed amount approximately 2,052 yuan.','Regarding the Qintai Heyuan property, both parties acknowledge that a dispute arose over the parties’ oral promises concerning ramp repairs and cleaning fees; because the disputed item was not recorded in the property handover form, the parties were unable to agree on how the deposit, repair, or service costs should be allocated.','The draft contract and recording summary in the Qintai Heyuan case file corroborate one another with the time records. On this basis, the court held that key matters capable of being included in the attachment should primarily be governed by the written agreement and strictly scrutinized promises made by the parties that were not included in the contract.','The key holding is that key matters that can be included in an appendix should primarily be governed by written agreements; in the Qintai Heyuan lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadline cannot be based solely on oral statements.','The matter concerning the written attachment for Qintai Heyuan was ultimately resolved by “determining liability in accordance with valid written terms.” After calculation, the supported amount was 1,433 yuan; the portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Support','Wuhan, lease, written attachment, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_33581e25','(2025) Hubei 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 28917','Qintai Qingting Noise-Related Rent Reduction Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-10-28','Tenant Ye, Landlord Chen','Qintai Qingting rent reduction dispute over noise: Prolonged construction noise exceeded the reasonable tolerance level for everyday living; the disputed amount was approximately 5132 yuan.','This case arose from the noise-related rent-reduction issue after the handover of Qintai Qingting. The tenant submitted materials alleging that prolonged construction noise exceeded a reasonable level of tolerance for normal living, while the landlord explained its handling by stating that “the disputed item was not recorded on the property handover form.”','Regarding the noise-related rent reduction issue at Qintai Qingting, the court relied primarily on construction notices and continuous audio recordings, while considering the condition at handover and subsequent remedial measures; a landlord who knows of a significant impact but fails to disclose it should bear liability.','The court held in the Qintai Qingting case that a landlord should bear liability when, despite knowing of a material impact, the landlord fails to disclose it, and that key costs and living conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Qintai Qingting: reduce the rent for the affected period at its discretion; the established losses shall be counted toward liability in the amount of 982 yuan, and the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Support','Wuhan, lease, noise-related rent reduction, accessibility');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_9f3b8033','(2023) E 0106 Civil First Instance No. 5521','Moshui Lake Apartment Deposit Refund Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-11-14','Tenant Shen, Landlord Tang','Moshuihu Apartment deposit refund dispute: The lessor withheld the deposit on the grounds of deep cleaning, with the disputed amount approximately 33194 yuan.','After moving into Moshuihu Apartment, Tenant Shen claimed that the landlord withheld the security deposit on the grounds of deep cleaning. During the handover of Moshuihu Apartment, the property handover form did not record the disputed item, and the parties consequently disagreed over the timing of the notice and the scope of the costs.','With respect to Moshui Lake Apartment, the court reviewed the transfer records and handover photographs. These materials establish the course of the transaction. Considering the sequence in which the parties performed, it may be concluded that ordinary signs of use cannot automatically be deemed damage, and unsupported oral assertions shall not serve as the primary basis.','Moshuihu Apartment case confirmation: Traces of normal use cannot automatically be deemed damage; the issues involving door width, repair costs, and service fees should all be determined based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the Moshuihu apartment dispute, the court ordered the return of the portion of the deposit corresponding to unproven losses; the amount supported by documentation was determined to be 18368 yuan, and the remaining claims were handled separately.','Rejected','Wuhan, lease, deposit return, security deposit');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_3828b316','(2025) E01 Civil First Instance No. 26969','Moshui Lake Jiayuan Repair Liability Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_intermediate','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-11-28','Tenant Lin, Landlord Luo','Moshui Lake Jiayuan repair liability dispute: After water seepage occurred in the bathroom, the parties disagreed over the repair period, involving a disputed amount of approximately 27436 yuan.','After the tenancy relationship at Moshuihu Jiayuan was established, an issue arose: “Following water seepage in the bathroom, the parties disagreed over the repair deadline.” Upon discovering the issue, the tenant promptly sent written notice, after which the tenant and landlord each submitted evidence regarding the written attachments and actual losses.','In hearing the dispute over repair liability at Moshuihu Jiayuan, the judicial panel first verified the repair request orders and on-site inspection reports, then compared them with the contract appendices and notice records. Based on the evidence currently available, the landlord should bear corresponding liability for failing to make timely repairs after becoming aware of the issue, with liability apportioned according to the actual impact.','The key point of the judgment is that a landlord bears corresponding liability if, after becoming aware of an issue, they fail to make repairs promptly; in the Moshuihu Jiayuan lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadline cannot be left to oral statements alone.','The Moshui Lake Jiayuan repair liability matter was ultimately resolved by requiring payment of the repair costs and compensation for reasonable losses; upon calculation, the supported amount was 15959 yuan, and any portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, repair responsibility, repairs');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_c8108c8c','(2023) E 0102 Civil First-Instance No. 16084','Moshui Lake Lixiang doorway-width representation contract dispute case','court_wh_jiangan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-05-19','Tenant Zhou, Landlord Xu','Moshui Lake Lixiang doorway-width representation dispute: The intermediary verbally promised a certain entrance-door width, but the measurement at delivery did not match, involving a disputed amount of approximately 14872 yuan.','Regarding the Moshuihu Lixiang property, the parties confirm that the intermediary verbally promised a certain entrance-door width, but the measurement at handover did not match; because the landlord submitted repair quotations and proof of payment, they were unable to reach agreement on how the deposit, repair costs, or service fees should be allocated.','The chat records and doorway-width measurement photos with timestamps in the Moshui Lake Lixiang case corroborate one another. On this basis, the court held that key residential conditions, when they form the basis for entering into a contract, must be truthfully disclosed, and strictly scrutinized promises between the parties that were not included in the contract.','In the Moshuihu Lixiang case, the court clarified that key residential conditions forming the basis for entering into a contract must be truthfully disclosed, and that key fees and residential conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Moshuihu Lixiang: refund the service fee and adjust the liability for breach of contract; the verified losses are assessed at 10072 yuan and assigned as liability, while the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Partial support','Wuhan, rental, door width details, repairs');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_26476ac3','(2023) E 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 24739','Moshuihu Community Elevator Shutdown Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-12-15','Tenant Gu, landlord Han','Moshuihu Community elevator shutdown dispute: elevators in a high-rise residential building were out of service for an extended period, affecting normal use, with the amount in dispute approximately 24685 yuan.','This case arose from an elevator shutdown issue after the handover of Moshuihu Community. The tenant submitted materials stating that the prolonged shutdown of the elevator in the high-rise residential building affected normal use, while the landlord explained its handling by saying that “the landlord submitted repair quotations and proof of payment.”','For the elevator shutdown issue at Moshuihu Shequ, the court primarily relied on property-management notices and maintenance records, considered the handover condition and subsequent remedial measures, and held that rent may be reduced at the court’s discretion when the prolonged shutdown reaches a level that affects habitability.','The Moshuihu Community case confirmed that rent may be reduced at the court’s discretion when a prolonged shutdown reaches a level that affects habitation; issues involving door width, repairs, and service fees should all be determined based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the Moshuihu community dispute, the court ordered a partial rent reduction for the affected period; the amount supported by documentation was determined to be 10496 yuan, and the remaining claims were handled separately.','Support','Wuhan, rental, elevator outage, service fee');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_86318ac6','(2023) E 0106 Civil First Instance No. 2594','Contract Dispute Case Concerning Occupation of the Moshuihu Xinyuan Passageway','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-03-18','Tenant Chen and landlord Wu','Dispute over Occupation of the Moshuihu Xinyuan Passageway: The public ramp was repeatedly occupied by electric bicycles and miscellaneous items, with the disputed amount approximately 20,125 yuan.','After moving into Moshuihu Xinyuan, tenant Chen claimed that the public ramp was repeatedly obstructed by electric bicycles and miscellaneous items. During the handover at Moshuihu Xinyuan, the parties attempted to resolve the matter through property-management coordination but failed to reach an agreement, and consequently disputed the timing of the notice and the scope of the costs.','With respect to Moshui Lake Xinyuan, the court reviewed the on-site video and property-management complaint records. These materials establish the course of the transaction. Considering the sequence in which the parties performed, it may be concluded that the management party should take reasonable cleaning measures after receiving a report, and unsupported oral assertions shall not serve as the primary basis.','The key holding is that after receiving a report, the management party should take reasonable cleanup measures; in the Moshuihu Xinyuan lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadlines cannot rely solely on oral statements.','The Moshui Lake Xinyuan passageway occupation matter was ultimately resolved by requiring the obstruction to be cleared by a specified deadline and inspections to be improved; upon calculation, the supported amount was 10483 yuan, and any portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, passageway obstruction, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_304e9098','(2023) E 01 Civil First-Instance No. 24275','Moshuihu Huating intermediary service fee contract dispute case','court_wh_intermediate','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-12-17','Tenant Tang, Landlord Jiang','Moshuihu Huating intermediary service fee dispute: After the contract was not finalized, the intermediary charged the full service fee, with the disputed amount approximately 14283 yuan.','After the lease relationship at Moshuihu Huating was established, a problem arose in which the intermediary charged the full service fee after the contract was not finalized. The intermediary failed to provide complete records of the service process, and the tenant and lessor subsequently submitted their respective evidence regarding the written attachments and actual losses.','In hearing the dispute over an agency service fee at Moshuihu Huating, the judicial panel first verified the service agreement and property viewing records, then compared them with the contract appendices and notice records. Based on the evidence currently available, if the services were not fully performed, the fee should be determined in light of the actual amount of work completed, with liability apportioned according to the actual impact.','In the Moshuihu Huating case, the court clarified that when services are not fully performed, fees should be determined based on the actual amount of work completed, and that key fees and residential conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Moshuihu Huating: refund service fees for services not actually provided; the verified losses are assessed at 6539 yuan and assigned as liability, while the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Partial support','Wuhan, rental, agency service fee, repairs');
