INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_1c38f80d','(2025) E 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 21634','Moshui Lake Neighborhood identity-document contract dispute case','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-07-11','Tenant Xu, Landlord Shen','Moshui Lake Neighborhood identity-document dispute: Before signing the contract, the intermediary requested too many photos of identity documents, involving a disputed amount of approximately 18232 yuan.','This case arose from an identity-document issue after the handover of Moshuihu Neighborhood. The tenant submitted materials stating that the agency had requested too many photos of identity documents before signing the lease, while the landlord explained its handling by saying that “the disputed items were not recorded on the property handover form.”','For the identity-document issue at Moshuihu Linli, the court primarily relied on the information-collection page and chat records, considered the handover condition and subsequent remedial measures, and held that rental verification should follow the principles of clear purpose and minimum necessity.','The key holding is that lease verification should follow the principles of purpose specification and data minimization; in the Moshuihu Neighborhood lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadlines cannot rely solely on oral statements.','The Moshui Lake Neighborhood identity-document matter was ultimately handled by “deleting irrelevant materials and ceasing further processing.” Upon calculation, the supported amount was 14548 yuan; any portion beyond the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, identity documents, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_29b39ca4','(2024) E 0106 Civil First Instance No. 22374','Moshui Lake Xiaoyuan Written Annex Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-02-03','Tenant Han, landlord Lin','Moshui Lake Xiaoyuan written annex dispute: The parties disputed their oral promises regarding ramp repairs and cleaning fees, involving a disputed amount of approximately 2525 yuan.','After moving into Moshuihu Xiaoyuan, tenant Han claimed that the parties disputed their oral agreement regarding ramp repairs and cleaning fees. During the handover of Moshuihu Xiaoyuan, the parties attempted to coordinate through property management but failed to reach an agreement, and consequently disagreed over the timing of the notice and the scope of the fees.','With respect to Moshui Lake Courtyard, the court reviewed the contract draft and audio-recording summary. These materials establish the course of the transaction. Considering the sequence in which the parties performed, it may be concluded that key matters capable of being included in an attachment should be based primarily on a written agreement, and unsupported oral assertions shall not serve as the primary basis.','In the Moshuihu Xiaoyuan case, the court clarified that key matters capable of being included in an appendix should primarily be governed by written agreements, and that key fees and residential conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Moshuihu Xiaoyuan: determine liability in accordance with the valid written terms; the verified losses are assessed at 872 yuan and assigned as liability, while the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Rejected','Wuhan, lease, written attachment, accessibility');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_73692d66','(2025) E01 Civil First Instance No. 28343','Moshui Lake Residential Community Noise and Rent Reduction Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_intermediate','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-04-12','Tenant Wu, Landlord Zhou','Moshui Lake Residential Community noise and rent reduction dispute: Long-term construction noise exceeded the reasonable tolerance level for normal living, involving a disputed amount of approximately 12,356 yuan.','After the tenancy at Moshui Lake Residential Community was established, the issue arose that “long-term construction noise exceeded the reasonable tolerance level for normal living.” After discovering the issue, the lessee promptly sent written notice, and the lessee and lessor subsequently each presented evidence regarding the written attachments and actual losses.','In hearing the dispute over a rent reduction for noise at the Moshuihu Residential Community, the judicial panel first verified the construction notices and continuous audio recordings, then compared them with the contract appendices and notice records. Based on the evidence currently available, the landlord should bear liability if, despite knowing of the significant impact, it failed to disclose it, with liability apportioned according to the actual impact.','Moshui Lake Residential Community case confirmation: When a lessor knows of a major impact but fails to disclose it, the lessor should bear responsibility; the issues involving door width, repairs, and service fees should all be determined based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the Moshuihu residential area dispute, the court ordered a discretionary reduction or waiver of rent for the affected period; the amount supported by documentation was determined to be 9357 yuan, and the remaining claims were handled separately.','Support','Wuhan, lease, noise-related rent reduction, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_afd095c8','(2025) E0102 Civil First Instance Case No. 10672','Moshui Lake Dormitory Deposit Return Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_jiangan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2025-06-13','Tenant Jiang, Landlord Gu','Moshui Lake Dormitory deposit return dispute: The lessor withheld the deposit on the grounds of deep cleaning, involving a disputed amount of approximately 4100 yuan.','Regarding the Moshuihu Dormitory property, the parties confirm that the landlord withheld the deposit on the grounds of deep cleaning; because the landlord submitted repair quotations and proof of payment, they were unable to reach agreement on how the deposit, repair costs, or service fees should be allocated.','The transfer records and handover photographs in the Moshui Lake Dormitory case file corroborate the time records. On this basis, the court held that ordinary signs of use could not automatically be deemed damage and strictly scrutinized the parties’ commitments that were not included in the contract.','The key point of the judgment is that signs of normal use cannot automatically be deemed damage; in the Moshuihu dormitory rental, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadline cannot be based solely on oral statements.','The Moshui Lake Dormitory deposit return matter was ultimately resolved by returning the portion of the deposit for which no loss was proven; upon calculation, the supported amount was 2163 yuan, and any portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Rejected','Wuhan, Rental, Deposit Refund, Service Fee');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_f6ec40f8','(2024) E 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 10797','Moshui Lake Yating maintenance-responsibility contract dispute case','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-12-22','Tenant Ye, Landlord Chen','Moshui Lake Yating maintenance-responsibility dispute: After water seepage in the bathroom, the parties disagreed over the repair deadline, involving a disputed amount of approximately 9367 yuan.','This case arose from a repair-responsibility issue after the handover of Moshuihu Yating. The tenant submitted materials stating that the parties disagreed over the repair deadline after water seepage occurred in the bathroom, while the landlord explained its handling by saying that “the tenant promptly sent written notice after discovering the issue.”','For the repair liability issue at Moshuihu Yating, the court primarily relied on the repair requests and on-site inspection report, considered the handover condition and subsequent remedial measures, and held that the landlord bears corresponding liability when, after becoming aware of the issue, it failed to make timely repairs.','In the Moshuihu Yating case, the court clarified that a landlord who fails to make timely repairs after becoming aware of the issue should bear the corresponding liability, and that key fees and residential conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Moshuihu Yating: bear the repair costs and compensate for reasonable losses; the verified losses are assessed at 7343 yuan and assigned as liability, while the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Partial support','Wuhan, rental, repair responsibility, door width');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_4d10820e','(2024) E 0106 Civil First Instance No. 23426','Contract Dispute Case Concerning the Representation of Doorway Width at Moshuihu Chunxiao','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-12-26','Tenant Shen, Landlord Tang','Dispute over the Representation of Doorway Width at Moshuihu Chunxiao: The agent verbally promised a certain entrance doorway width, but measurements at handover did not match, with the disputed amount approximately 14,475 yuan.','Tenant Shen moved into Moshui Lake Chunxiao and later claimed that the agent had orally promised a certain entrance-door width, but the measurement at handover did not match; during the handover at Moshui Lake Chunxiao, the tenant promptly sent written notice after discovering the issue, whereupon the parties disputed the timing of the notice and the scope of the costs.','With respect to Moshui Lake Chunxiao, the court reviewed the chat records and photographs measuring the doorway width. These materials establish the course of the transaction. Considering the sequence in which the parties performed, it may be concluded that key living conditions, when they form the basis for entering into the contract, should be truthfully disclosed, and unsupported oral assertions shall not serve as the primary basis.','The Moshuihu Chunxiao Case Confirms: When key residential conditions form the basis for entering into a contract, they must be truthfully disclosed; issues concerning doorway width, maintenance fees, and service fees should all be determined based on the specific written evidence.','Regarding the Moshuihu Chunxiao dispute, the court ordered the service fee to be refunded and adjusted the contractual liability for breach; the amount supported by documentation was determined to be 2360 yuan, and the remaining claims were handled separately.','Partial support','Wuhan, rental, door width explanation, deposit');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_0e45c7ca','(2024) E 01 Civil First Instance No. 22640','Moshuihu Heyuan elevator outage contract dispute case','court_wh_intermediate','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-01-26','Tenant Lin, Landlord Luo','Moshuihu Heyuan elevator outage dispute: The prolonged shutdown of elevators in a high-rise residence affected normal use, with the disputed amount approximately 33663 yuan.','After the lease relationship at Moshuihu Heyuan was established, a problem arose in which the prolonged shutdown of elevators in a high-rise residence affected normal use. The property handover form did not record the disputed items, and the tenant and lessor subsequently submitted their respective evidence regarding the written attachments and actual losses.','In hearing the dispute over the elevator shutdown at Moshuihu Heyuan, the judicial panel first verified the property management notices and maintenance records, then compared them with the contract appendices and notice records. Based on the evidence currently available, rent may be reduced as appropriate when the prolonged shutdown reaches a level that affects habitability, with liability apportioned according to the actual impact.','The key point of the judgment is that rent may be reduced at the court''s discretion when a prolonged shutdown reaches a level that affects habitability; in the Moshuihu Heyuan lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadline cannot be left to oral statements alone.','The Moshuihu Heyuan elevator outage matter was ultimately resolved by reducing part of the rent according to the period affected. After calculation, the supported amount was 14366 yuan; any portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, elevator outage, accessibility');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_0e698fd7','(2023) E 0102 Civil First-Instance No. 17524','Moshuihu Qingting Passageway Occupation Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_jiangan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-05-02','Tenant Zhou, Landlord Xu','Moshuihu Qingting passageway occupation dispute: a public ramp was repeatedly occupied by electric bicycles and miscellaneous items, with the amount in dispute approximately 4410 yuan.','Regarding the Moshuihu Qingting property, the parties confirm that the common ramp was repeatedly obstructed by electric bicycles and miscellaneous items; because the landlord submitted repair quotations and proof of payment, they were unable to reach agreement on how the deposit, repair costs, or service fees should be allocated.','The on-site video and property-management complaint records in the Moshuihu Qingting case file corroborate the timeline, and the court therefore held that the management party should have taken reasonable cleanup measures after receiving the report and that promises not written into the contract should be scrutinized strictly.','In the Moshuihu Qingting case, the court clarified that the management party should take reasonable cleanup measures after receiving a report, and that key fees and residential conditions should be documented through contract appendices, handover forms, or notification records.','The court ruled regarding Moshuihu Qingting: complete the cleanup and improve inspections within a specified period; the verified losses are assessed at 2640 yuan and assigned as liability, while the parties shall continue performing the remainder of the contract.','Mediation','Wuhan, rental, passageway obstruction, deposit');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_711c2a12','(2023) E 0111 Civil First-Instance No. 27607','Qinghe Apartment Agency Service Fee Contract Dispute Case','court_wh_hongshan','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2023-11-11','Tenant Gu, landlord Han','Qinghe Apartment Agency Service Fee Dispute: After the contract was not concluded, the agency collected the full service fee, with the disputed amount being approximately 30413 yuan.','This case arose from an intermediary service-fee issue after the handover of Qinghe Apartment. The tenant submitted materials claiming that the agent had collected the full service fee after the contract was not concluded, while the landlord explained its handling of the matter by stating that “the tenant sent written notice promptly after discovering the problem.”','For the property agency service fee issue at Qinghe Apartment, the court relied primarily on the service agreement and property-viewing records, considered the handover condition and subsequent remedial measures, and held that when the services were not fully performed, the fee should be determined in light of the actual amount of work completed.','Qinghe Apartment case confirmation: When services have not been fully performed, the fee should be determined based on the actual amount of work; the door width, repair costs, and service fees involved should all be assessed based on specific written evidence.','Regarding the Qinghe apartment dispute, the court ordered a refund of service fees that were not actually incurred. The amount supported by documentation was determined to be 366 yuan, and the remaining claims will be handled separately.','Support','Wuhan, rental, agency service fee, service fee');
INSERT INTO cases(case_id,case_number,title,court_id,case_type,cause,judgment_date,parties,summary,facts,reasoning,holding,ruling,outcome,keywords) VALUES ('case_wh_a90db933','(2024) E 0106 Civil First Instance No. 19713','Qinghe Jiayuan early lease termination contract dispute case','court_wh_wuchang','Contract Dispute','Housing lease contract dispute','2024-04-13','Tenant Chen and landlord Wu','Qinghe Jiayuan early lease termination dispute: The tenant requested early termination due to changes in living conditions, involving approximately 29369 yuan.','After moving into Qinghe Jiayuan, tenant Chen claimed that the tenant sought early termination because of changed living conditions. During the handover at Qinghe Jiayuan, the landlord submitted repair quotations and proof of payment, leading the parties to disagree over the timing of notice and the scope of the costs.','With respect to Qinghe Jiayuan, the court reviewed the contract appendices and the correspondence emails. These materials can establish the course of the transaction. In conjunction with the order in which the parties performed, it may be determined that when the liquidated damages are excessively high and the losses are limited, they may be adjusted in accordance with the law, while oral statements unsupported by other evidence should not be treated as the primary basis.','The key point of the ruling is that when liquidated damages are excessively high and the losses are limited, they may be adjusted in accordance with the law; in the Qinghe Jiayuan lease, the deposit, accessibility facilities, and repair deadlines cannot rely solely on oral statements.','The Qinghe Jiayuan early lease termination matter was ultimately handled in accordance with “assuming appropriate responsibility based on actual losses.” Upon calculation, the supported amount was 11917 yuan; the portion exceeding the scope of the evidence was not supported.','Support','Wuhan, Early Lease Termination, Door Width');
